sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Straight lines which are parallel to the same straight line but do not lie in the same plane with it are also parallel to each other.
----
proof:

Let each of the straight lines {AB} and {CD} be parallel to {EF}, but not in the same plane with it.

I say that {AB} is parallel to {CD}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="270" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.9 diagram" src="propXI9.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // AB and CD are each parallel to EF; G is taken on EF, GH is drawn at
    // right angles to EF in the plane of EF and AB, GK likewise in the plane
    // of EF and CD. XI.4 puts EF at right angles to the plane of HG and GK,
    // XI.8 carries that to AB and CD, and XI.6 makes them parallel.
    //
    // In Joyce's oblique view H falls on AB and K on CD (H = A + G - E,
    // K = C + G - E), which is where AB and CD meet the plane through HG and
    // GK. Everything added is transparent: planeABFE and planeCDFE, the
    // planes through EF and AB and through EF and CD; planeHGK, the plane
    // through HG and GK. The right angles are angleMarkerRight squares:
    // HGF and KGF by construction, AHG and CKG once AB and CD are proved
    // at right angles to that plane (XI.Def.3). They draw in the projection.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, E free; D, F, G
    // lineSliders. G arrives with "Let a point G be taken", so it is
    // deferred. H and K are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","D","E","F","AB","CD","EF"];
    var GPT   = GIVEN.concat(["G"]);
    var GHv   = GPT.concat(["H","GH","planeABFE"]);
    var GKv   = GHv.concat(["K","GK","planeCDFE"]);
    var FIG   = GPT.concat(["H","GH","K","GK"]);
    var RT    = FIG.concat(["angHGF","angKGF"]);
    var PLN   = RT.concat(["planeHGK"]);
    var ABr   = PLN.concat(["angAHG"]);
    var BOTH  = ABr.concat(["angCKG"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XI.9",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;220,40",
            "B;point;free;90,40",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "C;point;free;210,160",
            "D';point;parallelogram;B,A,C;0;0",
            "D;point;lineSlider;C,D',80,160",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "E;point;free;160,120",
            "F';point;parallelogram;B,A,E;0;0",
            "F;point;lineSlider;E,F',30,120",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F",
            "G;point;lineSlider;EF,100,160",
            "H;point;parallelogram;A,E,G",
            "K;point;parallelogram;C,E,G",
            "GH;line;connect;G,H",
            "GK;line;connect;G,K",
            // Transparent highlight targets.
            "planeABFE;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,F,E;0;0;0;0",
            "planeCDFE;polygon;quadrilateral;C,D,F,E;0;0;0;0",
            "planeHGK;polygon;triangle;H,G,K;0;0;0;0",
            "angHGF;sector;angleMarkerRight;G,H,F",
            "angKGF;sector;angleMarkerRight;G,K,F",
            "angAHG;sector;angleMarkerRight;H,A,G",
            "angCKG;sector;angleMarkerRight;K,C,G"
        ],
        deferDraggables: ["G"],
        aliases: { "HG": "GH", "FE": "EF" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“Straight lines which are parallel to the same straight line”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","EF"] },
            { text: "“but do not lie in the same plane with it”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["EF"] },
            { text: "“are also parallel to each other.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XI.9" }] },
            { text: "Let each of the straight lines {AB} and {CD} be parallel to {EF}, but not in the same plane with it.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","EF"] },
            { text: "I say that {AB} is parallel to {CD}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"] },
            { text: "Let a point {G} be taken at random on {EF},",
              visible: GPT,
              highlighted: ["G","EF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "G", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and from it draw {GH} in the {plane|planeABFE} through {EF} and {AB} at right angles to {EF},",
              visible: GHv.concat(["angHGF"]),
              highlighted: ["GH","planeABFE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "GH",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "H",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "angHGF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "GH at right angles to EF", ref: "I.11" }] },
            { text: "and {GK} in the {plane|planeCDFE} through {EF} and {CD} again at right angles to {EF}.",
              visible: GKv.concat(["angHGF","angKGF"]),
              highlighted: ["GK","planeCDFE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "GK",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "K",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "angKGF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "GK at right angles to EF", ref: "I.11" }] },
            { text: "Now, since {EF} is at right angles to each of the straight lines {GH} and {GK},",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["EF","GH","GK","angHGF","angKGF"] },
            { text: "therefore {EF} is also at right angles to the {plane|planeHGK} through {GH} and {GK}.",
              visible: PLN,
              highlighted: ["EF","planeHGK"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "planeHGK", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "at right angles to two lines at their section", ref: "XI.4" }] },
            { text: "And {EF} is parallel to {AB},",
              visible: PLN,
              highlighted: ["EF","AB"] },
            { text: "therefore {AB} is also at right angles to the {plane|planeHGK} through {HG} and {GK}.",
              visible: ABr,
              highlighted: ["AB","planeHGK","angAHG"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angAHG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "parallel to a line at right angles to a plane", ref: "XI.8" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason {CD} is also at right angles to the {plane|planeHGK} through {HG} and {GK}.",
              visible: BOTH,
              highlighted: ["CD","planeHGK","angCKG"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angCKG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore each of the straight lines {AB} and {CD} is at right angles to the {plane|planeHGK} through {HG} and {GK}.",
              visible: BOTH,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","planeHGK"] },
            { text: "But if two straight lines are at right angles to the same plane, then the straight lines are parallel.",
              visible: BOTH,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","planeHGK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "two lines at right angles to one plane", ref: "XI.6" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {AB} is parallel to {CD}.",
              visible: BOTH,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"] },
            { text: "Therefore, straight lines which are parallel to the same straight line",
              visible: FIG,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","EF"] },
            { text: "but do not lie in the same plane with it are also parallel to each other.",
              visible: FIG,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.9") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.11": "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI11/",
        "XI.4": "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI4/",
        "XI.6": "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI6/",
        "XI.8": "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI8/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Let a point {G} be taken at random on {EF}, and from it draw {GH} in the plane through {EF} and {AB} at right angles to {EF}, and {GK} in the plane through {EF} and {CD} again at right angles to {EF}. [!just I.11]

Now, since {EF} is at right angles to each of the straight lines {GH} and {GK}, therefore {EF} is also at right angles to the plane through {GH} and {GK}. [!just XI.4]

And {EF} is parallel to {AB}, therefore {AB} is also at right angles to the plane through {HG} and {GK}. [!just XI.8]

For the same reason {CD} is also at right angles to the plane through {HG} and {GK}. Therefore each of the straight lines {AB} and {CD} is at right angles to the plane through {HG} and {GK}.

But if two straight lines are at right angles to the same plane, then the straight lines are parallel. Therefore {AB} is parallel to {CD}. [!just XI.6]

Therefore, *straight lines which are parallel to the same straight line but do not lie in the same plane with it are also parallel to each other.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

Note that this proposition is the three-dimensional analogue to proposition @I.30.

#### The Varignon parallelogram of space quadrilaterals

<figure class="diagram rdiagram">
<canvas id="canvas_1" width="270" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="Varignon parallelogram" src="propXI9a.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Guide figure: hover refs only, no slides. The sides AB..DA, the
    // parallelogram's sides EF..HE and the undrawn EG, FH are transparent
    // targets; EFGHt is a faceless twin of the filled EFGH, which would be
    // raised over AC and BD if highlighted (#140).
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_1",
        background: "0,0,100",
        title: "Varignon parallelogram",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;110,40",
            "B;point;free;45,210",
            "C;point;free;220,130",
            "D;point;free;210,210",
            "ABCD;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;black;0",
            "E;point;midpoint;A,B",
            "F;point;midpoint;B,C",
            "G;point;midpoint;C,D",
            "H;point;midpoint;D,A",
            "EFGH;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,G,H;0;0;black;random",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C;0;0;gray",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D;0;0;gray",
            // Transparent highlight targets.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C;0;0;0",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D;0;0;0",
            "DA;line;connect;D,A;0;0;0",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F;0;0;0",
            "FG;line;connect;F,G;0;0;0",
            "GH;line;connect;G,H;0;0;0",
            "HE;line;connect;H,E;0;0;0",
            "EG;line;connect;E,G;0;0;0",
            "FH;line;connect;F,H;0;0;0",
            "EFGHt;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,G,H;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        aliases: { "HG": "GH", "EH": "HE" }
    });
</script>
</figure>

Consider a quadrilateral {ABCD} whose four vertices may or may not lie in a plane. Let {E}, {F}, {G}, and {H} be the midpoints of the sides {AB}, {BC}, {CD}, and {DA}, respectively. Then the quadrilateral {EFGH|EFGHt} lies in a plane and is a parallelogram, called the Varignon parallelogram. Varignon (1654–1722) showed the area of a planar quadrilateral is twice the area of this parallelogram.

The proof that {EFGH|EFGHt} is a parallelogram relies on this proposition XI.9 to show the sides are parallel, since it is readily shown that both {EF} and {HG} are parallel to the line {AC}, and both {FG} and {EH} are parallel to the line {BD}.

As a corollary, it follows that the lines joining the midpoints of an arbitrary quadrilateral are concurrent and bisect each other, even if the four sides of the quadrilateral do not lie in a plane. (These are the lines {EG} and {FH} which are not drawn in the diagram.)

#### Use of this proposition

This proposition is used in the proof of the next proposition as well as others in this and the next book.
